# Project Notes

## Dataset

The project uses the Cisco Networking Academy Movies dataset containing 4,535 films released between 2000 and 2017.

## Data Preparation

The Excel workflow reports 3,420 films retained after removing records with missing budget/revenue values.

Calculated metrics include:

- Profit
- ROI
- Profit Margin
- Budget Category

## SQL Analysis

The SQL analysis contains 10 core queries and one bonus query.

The queries cover:

- Dataset overview
- Revenue performance
- ROI
- Annual trends
- Language analysis
- Budget tiers
- Critical and commercial success
- Popularity
- Runtime
- Profit by year
- English vs non-English comparison

## SQL Compatibility

The SQL script is primarily MySQL-compatible.

For SQLite, the project SQL comments document replacements for:

- `FORMAT()`
- `YEAR()`

## ROI Interpretation

The Excel workbook reports an average ROI of 234,252.8%.

This value is extremely high because percentage ROI can become very large when production budgets are small.

Therefore, ROI should be interpreted as a comparative efficiency metric rather than a typical industry-wide average.
